ets put  in critical condition told by doctors  that his son won't survive silas makes a  desperate attempt to save his life and  he turns to a signs he doesn't fully  understand now joe morton has dabbled  with this kind of technology before and  it's inspired casting to bring him into  this film when he started miles dyson  and terminator 2. really nice little  easter egg there and silas ends up  fusing his son with a mother box which  resurrects him victor absolutely hates  this change and it's clear that early on  he feels like it's a curse that he can't  escape from there are languages in his  head that he doesn't understand a  constant buzzing and connections to  almost every electronic device on earth  it really makes you question what you  would do if the person you loved was at  that store and i love how there's this  duality in the scene you have silas who  did whatever he could to try and save  his son and on the opposite side of this  you get victor who very much doesn't  want to be alive like this towards the  end of the film he's even tempted with  being with his family once more and  gaining somewhat normality inside the  mother box though this is an illusion  it's something that he could have easily  have given into because that's what his  heart desired at the channel we often  talk about how in order to be a hero  that one has to sacrifice what they want  and victor making this choice at the end  brings the ark set up here full circle  now just in the same way we question  whether he would bring someone back from  the brink if it doomed them to a  half-life we also put ourselves in  victor's shoes we discover that he has  unlimited power in the world of ones and  zeroes and that almost everything is now  under his control this includes the  stock market currency weapons cars  tamagotchis bank accounts the tinder  profile and it all rests in his hands  joe morton has created skynet again and  you didn't listen you bloody didn't  listen however what 