ow he did when his  mother was hit by a car cyborg  definitely goes through the most losses  in the movie as both of his parents die  and he's left alone in the world without  their guidance that's why the temptation  at the end of the film is so endearing  and after flash runs back in time he's  transported inside the mother box which  is where he comes face to face with them  amongst the nightmare hellscape of a  world taken over by darkseid they  promised to make him whole again and say  that he'll never be alone but vic  responds with  and i'm not this  it finally shows acceptance for what's  happened as well as the fact that he's  found kinship amongst the rest of the  league once an outcast that was feared  he's now found self-acceptance and also  a new family to be a part of it really  brings everything full circle and makes  for some amazing character growth that  plants him as the heart of the movie to  me it's the perfect way to introduce the  character while setting up what he ends  up becoming at the end of the film and i  absolutely love this scene obviously i'd  love to hear your thoughts on it so make  sure you comment below and let me know  if you want something else to watch then  make sure you check out project justice  league which will be linked on screen  right now it's from our friends over at  the four nerds network and it kind of  goes over the original plans for the  justice league sequels really really  nice fan made series so definitely go  head over there right after this without  the way thanks for sitting through the  video i'm paul i'll see you in the next  one take care peace

